# What `vercel` from the command line must not upload.
#
# The deploy that matters is the one GitHub triggers: Vercel clones the repo and
# builds it there, so nothing is uploaded from here at all. This file is for the
# times somebody runs the CLI anyway.
#
# Without it the CLI sends the working directory as it stands — node_modules and
# the built output included — which is twelve megabytes and thousands of files,
# and the free tier stops accepting uploads after five thousand in a day. None of
# it is needed: Vercel runs npm install and npm run build itself.
node_modules
out
.next
.vercel
